# Compiled artefacts that must never go through end-of-line conversion. Git's
# NUL-byte heuristic would usually catch these, but a rule is a guarantee and a
# heuristic is a bet — with autocrlf on, a mis-detected .wasm would be corrupted
# silently at checkout and only fail when instantiated.
*.wasm  binary
*.cwasm binary
*.exe   binary

# Documents whose exact BYTES are a contract with another program, pinned to LF so a Windows
# checkout and a Linux CI runner serve and hash the same thing.
#   * the served leaf-script profile — the server's ETag is a sha256 of these bytes, and its
#     `preambleSha256` is verified by the consumer before anything runs, so a checkout that
#     rewrote its newlines would hand two machines two different documents;
#   * the vendored copy of OAIY's schema — scriptProfile.test.ts recomputes its git blob hash
#     and compares it to the recorded one, which only holds if the copy is byte-identical.
formlogic/backend/resources/formlogic-script-profile.json  text eol=lf
formlogic/ui/src/lib/oaiy/vendored/script-profile.schema.json  text eol=lf
